From 32bccc748cca5e4a8ee7771a1f63a30b0f46e661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:23:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] microblaze: save the argument registers when no parameter
 is named

C23 allows a variadic function with no named parameters, "void f (...)".
Its type has no TYPE_ARG_TYPES, so the prologue's test for a varargs
function fails and r5-r10 are never stored to their stack slots.  va_arg
then reads whatever was there: gcc.c-torture/execute/pr117432.c fails at
every optimization level.

Also test TYPE_NO_NAMED_ARGS_STDARG_P.  The loop already starts at r5
when there is no named parameter.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/microblaze.cc (microblaze_expand_prologue):
	Save the argument registers for a function with no named
	parameters.
---
 gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
index 398c8ffa7..9cbf3fded 100644
--- a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
@@ -3009,6 +3009,7 @@ microblaze_expand_prologue (void)
   if (((TYPE_ARG_TYPES (fntype) != 0
 	&& (TREE_VALUE (tree_last (TYPE_ARG_TYPES (fntype)))
 	    != void_type_node))
+       || TYPE_NO_NAMED_ARGS_STDARG_P (fntype)
        || (arg_name != 0
 	   && ((arg_name[0] == '_'
 		&& strcmp (arg_name, "__builtin_va_alist") == 0)
